%U A400187 1261,1379,1382,1520,1526,1645,1652,1657,1660,1786,1793,1939,1948,1952,2099,2104,2107,2110,2417,2425,2440,2444,2606,2608,2611,2786
%N A400187 Walk along the hexagonal spiral, with its cells numbered starting at 0, as in A395362. Three players, Black, Cyan, and Red, take turns. When it is Black's's turn, he places a (Glinski) queen at the smallest unoccupied cell not attacked by an existing Cyan or Red queen; when it is Cyan's turn, he places a queen at the smallest unoccupied cell not attacked by an existing Black or Red queen, and when it is Red's turn, he places a queen at the smallest unoccupied cell not attacked by an existing Black or Cyan queen. Sequence lists cells occupied by Cyan queens.
%C A400187 These are Glinski queens, as in hexagonal chess (see A396292).
%C A400187 There is a subtle point about the definition. Because the players take turns placing queens, the spiral is not filled in consecutively. To obtain the sequence, one must first fill in the whole spiral, and then return to the start, and record the Cyan queens that are encountered as one walks along the spiral.
